## PROJECT OVERVIEW
Browser-based CAD tool generating parametric window configurations using Maker.js library.
Outputs professional DXF files for manufacturing workflows.

## CRITICAL RULE: MAKER.JS FIRST
**ALWAYS research Maker.js documentation/methods online before implementing solutions.**
- Maker.js provides specialized CAD primitives (lines, arcs, beziers, paths, models)
- DO NOT assume vanilla JS/Canvas solutions exist - Maker.js likely has built-in methods
- Official docs: https://maker.js.org/docs/
- Check for: model operations, path manipulation, measurement, boolean operations, export formats

## KEY CAPABILITIES
- **Window Types**: Casement, fixed, custom mullion patterns
- **Parameters**: Width, height, frame thickness, glazing bar configurations
- **Output**: SVG preview + DXF export for CNC/manufacturing
- **Geometry**: Parametric frame profiles, Georgian bars, dimension annotations

## DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT
**ALL external libraries download to:** `01__ExternalDependencies/`

Current dependencies:
- `01__ExternalDependencies/maker.js/` - Core CAD engine (local)
- Bezier.js (CDN) - Curve mathematics for text rendering
- opentype.js (CDN) - TrueType font â†’ CAD geometry conversion

## MAKER.JS ARCHITECTURE PATTERNS
```javascript
// Models contain paths and nested models
const windowModel = {
    models: {
        frame: frameGeometry,
        mullions: mullionGeometry
    },
    paths: {
        cill: new makerjs.paths.Line([0,0], [width,0])
    },
    units: makerjs.unitType.Millimeter
};

// Export to DXF
const dxf = makerjs.exporter.toDXF(windowModel);
```

## CODING STYLE
Inherits ValeDesignSuite conventions from parent workspace `.cursorrules`:
- Regional structure with `// REGION | Description`
- Inline comments: `// <-- Explanation`
- Column-aligned constants and properties
- 4-space indentation within regions

## HTML/JAVASCRIPT REGION MARKERS
This project uses collapsible region markers for code organization within HTML `<script>` tags:

**Primary Format (Major Sections):**
```javascript
// =============================================================================
// REGION | Section Description
// =============================================================================
// Optional context/explanation lines
// =============================================================================

// ... code content ...

// endregion ===================================================================
```

**Secondary Format (Subsections):**
```javascript
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// REGION | Subsection Description
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ... code content ...

// endregion -------------------------------------------------------------------
```

**HTML Comment Format (for <head> sections):**
```html
<!-- ================================================================= -->
<!-- REGION | Section Description -->
<!-- ================================================================= -->

<!-- content -->

<!-- endregion ======================================================== -->
```

**Existing Regions in HTML:**
- External Dependencies (script loading)
- Global Configuration Constants
- Script Configs (UI/Viewport configuration objects)
- CadGenerator modules (Dynamic UI, Viewport)
- Global Helper Functions
- Math Functions
- CAD Functions (window geometry generation)
- UI Functions (interface building)
- Event Handling, Observers, Callbacks
- Render Pipeline
- Initialization

**Usage:** Wrap logically related code blocks in regions for improved collapsibility and navigation in IDEs that support code folding.

## WHEN IN DOUBT
1. Search "Maker.js [operation]" online (e.g., "Maker.js combine models")
2. Check Maker.js playground examples: https://maker.js.org/playground/
3. Review existing `WindowConfigurator__Feature__*.js` modules for patterns
4. Verify solution works with Maker.js model/path structure before vanilla JS

